IMPORT prelude

-- Mutual Assistance in Criminal Matters Act 2000 (Singapore) -- when Singapore may and must refuse a foreign request for assistance
-- (ss 16, 20, with the s 2 meaning of "Singapore offence"), production orders and the offence of not complying (ss 22, 25), what a
-- witness must answer and what use may be made of evidence taken for a foreign country (ss 21, 21A), sending a person abroad to
-- assist (s 26), the safe conduct of a person brought to Singapore (s 11), no penalty for refusing to attend (ss 10, 26(4), 40), and
-- the maximum penalties (ss 25, 28, 35(4)).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/MACMA2000.txt, with amendments to
-- Act 10 of 2025 (in force 15 September 2026, a Second Schedule entry) and Act 42 of 2024 (in force 28 March 2025) shown. The
-- arrangement of sections at the top of the deposit is out of step with the body (it numbers "Meaning of item subject to legal
-- privilege" as 1); the body's numbers are used here.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Cited by 9 of the 527 Singapore Acts deposited in this repository. SCOPED to the decision the Attorney-General makes on
-- a foreign request, and to what the Act asks of people in Singapore caught up in one. Not encoded: requests BY Singapore (Part 2,
-- beyond s 11), the content of a request (s 19), enforcement and registration of foreign confiscation orders (ss 29 to 32 and the
-- Third Schedule), transit custody (s 27), locating persons and service of process beyond s 40, notice to the Minister (s 41), and the
-- First and Second Schedules (which offences are listed is taken as a fact). Inchoate forms (conspiracy, incitement, attempt,
-- abetment) in the s 2 definitions are not modelled separately.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Mutual Assistance in Criminal Matters Act 2000 -- foreign requests`

§§ `2 -- Singapore offence`

-- s 2(1): "drug dealing offence" -- an offence "specified in the First Schedule". "serious offence" -- an offence "other than a drug
-- dealing offence" that "(i) is specified in the Second Schedule; or (ii) is punishable with imprisonment for a term which may extend
-- to 4 years or more". "Singapore offence" means "(a) a drug dealing offence; or (b) a serious offence".
GIVEN `in the First Schedule` IS A BOOLEAN, `in the Second Schedule` IS A BOOLEAN, `maximum imprisonment in years` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the offence is a serious offence` IF
        (NOT `in the First Schedule`)
    AND (`in the Second Schedule` OR `maximum imprisonment in years` AT LEAST 4)

GIVEN `in the First Schedule` IS A BOOLEAN, `in the Second Schedule` IS A BOOLEAN, `maximum imprisonment in years` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the offence is a Singapore offence` IF
        `in the First Schedule`
    OR  `the offence is a serious offence` `in the First Schedule` `in the Second Schedule` `maximum imprisonment in years`

§§ `16 -- which countries may have which assistance`

-- s 16(1): "(a) assistance under sections 21 and 27(1) and Divisions 7 and 8 may be provided to any foreign country; and (b)
-- assistance under section 27(2) and Divisions 2 (other than section 21), 3, 5 and 6 may only be provided to any prescribed foreign
-- country". (2): despite (1)(b), that assistance may go to a non-prescribed country, or to a prescribed one for an offence outside its
-- s 17 order, "if the appropriate authority of that country has given an undertaking ... that that country will comply with a future
-- request by Singapore to that country for similar assistance". (3): such a country "is deemed a prescribed foreign country".
DECLARE Assistance IS ONE OF
    `evidence taken by a Magistrate`
    `a statement taken by an authorised officer`
    `a production order`
    `attendance of a person abroad`
    `custody in transit`
    `enforcement of a confiscation order`
    `search and seizure`
    `locating a person`
    `service of process`

-- Division 2 is ss 21 to 25; 3 is s 26; 4 is ss 27, 28; 5 is ss 29 to 32; 6 is ss 33 to 36; 7 is s 37; 8 is ss 38 to 40.
GIVEN `the kind` IS AN Assistance
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Division of Part 3` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the kind`
    WHEN `evidence taken by a Magistrate` THEN 2
    WHEN `a statement taken by an authorised officer` THEN 2
    WHEN `a production order` THEN 2
    WHEN `attendance of a person abroad` THEN 3
    WHEN `custody in transit` THEN 4
    WHEN `enforcement of a confiscation order` THEN 5
    WHEN `search and seizure` THEN 6
    WHEN `locating a person` THEN 7
    OTHERWISE 8

-- "custody in transit" here is s 27(2) custody in Singapore, which is in s 16(1)(b); bare transit under s 27(1) is not modelled.
GIVEN `the kind` IS AN Assistance
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the assistance is open to any foreign country` IF
    CONSIDER `the kind`
    WHEN `evidence taken by a Magistrate` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `locating a person` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `service of process` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

DECLARE Request HAS
    `the assistance` IS AN Assistance
    `the country is prescribed for the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the country gave a reciprocity undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the country breached the treaty terms` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the offence is political` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the act is an offence only under military law` IS A BOOLEAN
    `there are grounds to believe in a persecution purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person was finally convicted, acquitted, pardoned or punished` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the offence lacks sufficient gravity` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the thing is unimportant or obtainable otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
    `assistance is contrary to the public interest` IS A BOOLEAN
    `assistance could prejudice a Singapore criminal matter` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the conduct would be a Singapore offence here` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the offence is a foreign tax evasion offence` IS A BOOLEAN
    `there is an Income Tax Act arrangement with the country` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the country undertook to limit use of the thing` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the country undertook to return or dispose of the thing` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a treaty provides for refusal` IS A BOOLEAN
    `assistance would prejudice someone's safety` IS A BOOLEAN
    `assistance would overburden Singapore's resources` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the request` IS A Request
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the assistance may be provided to the country` IF
        `the assistance is open to any foreign country` (`the request`'s `the assistance`)
    OR  `the request`'s `the country is prescribed for the offence`
    OR  `the request`'s `the country gave a reciprocity undertaking`

§§ `20 -- refusal of assistance`

-- s 20(1): a request "must be refused" if, in the AG's opinion: (a) the country failed to comply with the treaty or MOU; (b) the offence
-- is "of a political character"; (c) the act would be an offence "under the military law ... but not also under the ordinary criminal
-- law"; (d) "substantial grounds for believing" the request is to prejudice a person on account of "race, religion, sex, ethnic origin,
-- nationality or political opinions"; (e) the person has been "convicted, acquitted or pardoned" with all appeals expired or exhausted,
-- or "has undergone the punishment"; (f) the offence "is not an offence of sufficient gravity"; (g) the thing is "of insufficient
-- importance ... or could reasonably be obtained by other means"; (h) "contrary to public interest"; (k) it "could prejudice a
-- criminal matter in Singapore". Paragraphs (i) and (j) were deleted by Act 42 of 2024.
GIVEN `the request` IS A Request
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 20(1) requires refusal` IF
        `the request`'s `the country breached the treaty terms`
    OR  `the request`'s `the offence is political`
    OR  `the request`'s `the act is an offence only under military law`
    OR  `the request`'s `there are grounds to believe in a persecution purpose`
    OR  `the request`'s `the person was finally convicted, acquitted, pardoned or punished`
    OR  `the request`'s `the offence lacks sufficient gravity`
    OR  `the request`'s `the thing is unimportant or obtainable otherwise`
    OR  `the request`'s `assistance is contrary to the public interest`
    OR  `the request`'s `assistance could prejudice a Singapore criminal matter`

-- s 20(2A): a request "to obtain any thing under section 22 or 23 or Division 6 must be refused" if the country "(a) fails to undertake
-- that the thing will not be used for a matter other than the criminal matter ... except with the consent of the Attorney-General; or
-- (b) fails to undertake" to return, dispose of or otherwise handle the thing as the AG requests on conclusion of the matter.
GIVEN `the request` IS A Request
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the request is to obtain a thing` IF
    CONSIDER `the request`'s `the assistance`
    WHEN `a production order` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `search and seizure` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the request` IS A Request
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 20(2A) requires refusal` IF
        `the request is to obtain a thing` `the request`
    AND (    (NOT `the request`'s `the country undertook to limit use of the thing`)
         OR  (NOT `the request`'s `the country undertook to return or dispose of the thing`))

-- s 20(3): "a request ... for assistance under Division 2, 5 or 6 must be refused if ... the request relates to ... conduct which, if it
-- had occurred in Singapore, would not have constituted a Singapore offence". (4): not for Division 2 if the request relates to "a
-- foreign tax evasion offence of that country". (5): not for Division 5 or 6 if it is a foreign tax evasion offence AND an arrangement
-- "under section 49 or 105BA of the Income Tax Act 1947, or an international tax compliance agreement" has been made with that country.
GIVEN `the request` IS A Request
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the tax evasion exception applies` IF
        `the request`'s `the offence is a foreign tax evasion offence`
    AND (    `the Division of Part 3` (`the request`'s `the assistance`) EQUALS 2
         OR  `the request`'s `there is an Income Tax Act arrangement with the country`)

GIVEN `the request` IS A Request
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `dual criminality applies` IF
        `the Division of Part 3` (`the request`'s `the assistance`) EQUALS 2
    OR  `the Division of Part 3` (`the request`'s `the assistance`) EQUALS 5
    OR  `the Division of Part 3` (`the request`'s `the assistance`) EQUALS 6

GIVEN `the request` IS A Request
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 20(3) requires refusal` IF
        `dual criminality applies` `the request`
    AND (NOT `the request`'s `the conduct would be a Singapore offence here`)
    AND (NOT `the tax evasion exception applies` `the request`)

GIVEN `the request` IS A Request
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `refusal is mandatory` IF
        `section 20(1) requires refusal` `the request`
    OR  `section 20(2A) requires refusal` `the request`
    OR  `section 20(3) requires refusal` `the request`

-- s 20(2): a request "may be refused" (a) pursuant to a treaty or MOU; (b) if assistance would, or would be likely to, "prejudice the
-- safety of any person (whether in Singapore or elsewhere)"; (c) if it "would impose an excessive burden on the resources of
-- Singapore"; or (d) for assistance under ss 21 and 27(1) and Divisions 7 and 8, if the country is not prescribed and fails to give the
-- reciprocity undertaking.
GIVEN `the request` IS A Request
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Attorney-General may refuse` IF
        `refusal is mandatory` `the request`
    OR  `the request`'s `a treaty provides for refusal`
    OR  `the request`'s `assistance would prejudice someone's safety`
    OR  `the request`'s `assistance would overburden Singapore's resources`
    OR  (    `the assistance is open to any foreign country` (`the request`'s `the assistance`)
         AND (NOT `the request`'s `the country is prescribed for the offence`)
         AND (NOT `the request`'s `the country gave a reciprocity undertaking`))

-- Whether the assistance can be given at all: s 16 must allow it and s 20 must not forbid it.
GIVEN `the request` IS A Request
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the request can be granted` IF
        `the assistance may be provided to the country` `the request`
    AND (NOT `refusal is mandatory` `the request`)

§§ `21, 21A -- witnesses and the use of what they say`

-- s 21(6): the person to whom the foreign proceedings relate "is competent, but not compellable, to give evidence". (7): a witness "must
-- not be required to answer any question that the person could not be compelled to answer in those proceedings in that country".
GIVEN `is the person the foreign proceedings relate to` IS A BOOLEAN, `compellable on the question abroad` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the witness must answer the question` IF
    (NOT `is the person the foreign proceedings relate to`) AND `compellable on the question abroad`

-- s 21(9): evidence taken by a Magistrate "is not admissible in evidence, and must not be otherwise used, for the purposes of any
-- judicial proceedings, disciplinary proceedings, or other proceedings, in Singapore except a prosecution of the person who gave that
-- evidence for the offence of perjury, or contempt of court". s 21A(5): a statement taken by an authorised officer "is not admissible
-- in evidence, and must not be otherwise used, for the purposes of any judicial proceedings, disciplinary proceedings, or other
-- proceedings, in Singapore" -- with NO perjury or contempt exception.
DECLARE Material IS ONE OF
    `evidence given before a Magistrate under section 21`
    `a statement taken under section 21A`

DECLARE Use IS ONE OF
    `a perjury or contempt prosecution of its maker`
    `a Singapore prosecution of someone else`
    `Singapore disciplinary proceedings`

GIVEN `the material` IS A Material, `the use` IS A Use
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the material may be used in Singapore` IF
    CONSIDER `the material`
    WHEN `evidence given before a Magistrate under section 21` THEN
        CONSIDER `the use`
        WHEN `a perjury or contempt prosecution of its maker` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `22, 25 -- production orders`

-- s 22(4): the court may order production if "(a) there are reasonable grounds for suspecting that a specified person has carried on or
-- benefited from a foreign offence; (b) ... the thing ... (i) is likely to be of substantial value ... and (ii) does not consist of or
-- include items subject to legal privilege; and (c) ... it is not contrary to the public interest". (3): produce or give access "within
-- 7 days of the date of the order or any other period that the court considers appropriate". (2): against a financial institution or
-- VCC, the application "must be made only to the General Division of the High Court".
GIVEN `suspects a person benefited from a foreign offence` IS A BOOLEAN, `the thing is of substantial value` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the thing includes privileged items` IS A BOOLEAN, `production is not contrary to the public interest` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the court may make a production order` IF
        `suspects a person benefited from a foreign offence`
    AND `the thing is of substantial value`
    AND (NOT `the thing includes privileged items`)
    AND `production is not contrary to the public interest`

GIVETH A NUMBER
`the default days to comply with a production order` MEANS 7

-- s 25: an offence for a person who "(a) without reasonable excuse contravenes or fails to comply with an order under section 22; or (b)
-- in purported compliance ... produces ... any material known to the person to be false or misleading in a material particular without
-- -- (i) indicating ... that the material is false or misleading ...; or (ii) providing correct information ... if the person is in
-- possession of, or can reasonably acquire, the correct information". "Without (i) or (ii)" is read here as: neither was done. That
-- reading is an inference; the text does not say whether both are needed.
GIVEN `failed to comply` IS A BOOLEAN, `had a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN, `produced material known to be false` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `said it was false` IS A BOOLEAN, `gave the correct information` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person commits the section 25 offence` IF
        (`failed to comply` AND (NOT `had a reasonable excuse`))
    OR  (`produced material known to be false` AND (NOT `said it was false`) AND (NOT `gave the correct information`))

-- s 25, s 28(1) (escape from transit custody under s 27(2)) and s 35(4) (hindering or obstructing execution of a s 34 search warrant):
-- each "a fine not exceeding $10,000 or ... imprisonment for a term not exceeding 2 years or ... both".
DECLARE Offence IS ONE OF
    `failing to comply with a production order`
    `escaping from transit custody`
    `obstructing a search warrant`

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `failing to comply with a production order` THEN 10000
    WHEN `escaping from transit custody` THEN 10000
    OTHERWISE 10000

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in years` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `failing to comply with a production order` THEN 2
    WHEN `escaping from transit custody` THEN 2
    OTHERWISE 2

§§ `26, 10, 40 -- attending abroad, and refusing to`

-- s 26(2): the AG may assist in arranging travel if satisfied that (a) the request relates to a criminal matter "involving a foreign
-- offence"; (b) the person "is capable of giving or providing evidence or assistance"; (c) the person "has freely consented"; (d) the
-- person is not "a prisoner within the meaning of section 2 of the Prisons Act 1933" or "otherwise under detention in a prescribed
-- institution"; and (e) the country "has given adequate undertakings" (no prosecution for earlier offences, no civil suit, no other
-- matter; evidence not used against the person except for perjury or contempt; return to Singapore).
GIVEN `involves a foreign offence` IS A BOOLEAN, `the person is capable of helping` IS A BOOLEAN, `the person freely consented` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the person is a prisoner or detained` IS A BOOLEAN, `adequate undertakings were given` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Attorney-General may arrange the person's travel` IF
        `involves a foreign offence`
    AND `the person is capable of helping`
    AND `the person freely consented`
    AND (NOT `the person is a prisoner or detained`)
    AND `adequate undertakings were given`

-- s 10 (a request by Singapore under s 9), s 26(4) (a foreign request to attend abroad) and s 40 (a foreign summons to appear as a
-- witness): the person "shall not" / "must not be subject to any penalty or liability or otherwise prejudiced in law by reason only of"
-- refusing or failing to consent, or to accept or comply with the summons -- s 40 adds "despite any contrary statement in the summons".
DECLARE Refusal IS ONE OF
    `refusing Singapore's request to come to Singapore`
    `refusing a foreign request to travel abroad`
    `ignoring a foreign witness summons served in Singapore`

GIVEN `the refusal` IS A Refusal
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person may be penalised for the refusal alone` IF
    CONSIDER `the refusal`
    WHEN `refusing Singapore's request to come to Singapore` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `refusing a foreign request to travel abroad` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `11 -- safe conduct of a person brought to Singapore`

-- s 11(1): a person in Singapore under a s 9 request must not be detained, prosecuted or punished for earlier offences, sued on earlier
-- acts, or made to assist in another criminal matter. (2): this "ceases to apply if (a) the person has left Singapore; or (b) the person
-- has had the opportunity of leaving Singapore and has remained ... otherwise than for (i) the purpose to which the request relates; or
-- (ii)" a matter certified by the AG in writing.
GIVEN `has left Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN, `had the opportunity to leave` IS A BOOLEAN, `stayed for the request or a certified matter` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the safe conduct immunity applies` IF
        (NOT `has left Singapore`)
    AND (    (NOT `had the opportunity to leave`)
         OR  `stayed for the request or a certified matter`)
